{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 10250,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this video Lego sent me some of their\nSaturn V rocket sets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this isn't a video about space - I actually\nwant to talk about the physics of how to keep"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17800,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tall things from shaking, like how to keep\nskyscrapers from swaying too much in the wind,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22000,
    "dDurationMs": 1130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or in an earthquake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23130,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The taller something is, the more liable it\nis to sway back and forth, so to demonstrate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27440,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this, the Saturn V seemed by far like the\nbest and coolest Lego set for the job (even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if not the most realistic)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32800,
    "dDurationMs": 2770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you don’t your tall thing to sway, either\nbecause you’re worried it’ll fall apart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35570,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or you’re worried it’ll freak out the\npeople inside, you could just make it stiffer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39010,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– either by adding more stuff or using more\nrigid materials – this isn’t always the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43490,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most elegant solution, and gets expensive\nfast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45830,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there’s another, clever solution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48100,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From a physics perspective, a tall thing like\na building is really an upside-down pendulum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52320,
    "dDurationMs": 3759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- when it gets bent a little bit to one side,\nthe building’s natural stiffness pulls it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56079,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back the other way, and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58129,
    "dDurationMs": 3011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there's a neat phenomenon that happens\nwith pendulums when you attach two of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61140,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "together with a spring: they start swapping\nenergy back and forth – first one oscillates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65990,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then both together, then the other has all\nthe oscillations, then the first again, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69970,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70970,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same thing happens with solid blocks and\nsprings, too, or any two oscillating things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75600,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are coupled together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77280,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a perfect frictionless simulation this\nenergy swapping will go on forever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81110,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the real world there's friction and\nair resistance and the spring itself might"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84909,
    "dDurationMs": 5121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heat up, causing the objects to lose energy,\nand the oscillations dampen over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90030,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this phenomenon is what you can use to\n‘discourage’ your upside-down pendulum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94290,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from shaking in ways you don’t want it to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96330,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A big tall object is going to want to sway\nback and forth at its own natural frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100460,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of swaying (which depends on its height, weight,\nand stiffness)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103720,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you then attach a smaller object to it\nthat can sway to and fro, and add a little"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107990,
    "dDurationMs": 4169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bit of friction, then any time the big object\ntrades its energy to the little object, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112159,
    "dDurationMs": 4201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little object loses the energy to friction\nrather than trading it back to the big object,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116360,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this dampens out the big object's oscillations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119450,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In practice, you normally put the little object\ninside the big object, which looks more like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123399,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this, but the principle is the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125729,
    "dDurationMs": 3531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you don’t want to use just any old little\nobject and any old spring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129260,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It turns out that for a particular big thing,\nthere’s an optimal combination of weight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132980,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and friction and spring strength for the little\nobject."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135780,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And only with your setup perfectly tuned will\nyou get the fastest possible loss of energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140410,
    "dDurationMs": 2159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the best slowing down of the shaking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142569,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s why this setup is called a “tuned\nmass damper” – “damper” because it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146849,
    "dDurationMs": 4311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dampens the swaying, and “tuned” because\nthe little object is specifically tuned to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151160,
    "dDurationMs": 4299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "steal energy from this particular big thing’s\nnatural tendency to swing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155459,
    "dDurationMs": 4011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which brings us to the Lego Saturn V rockets:\nin one of the rockets I’ve put a weighted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159470,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pendulum in the place the lunar module should\ngo, while the other just has the weights stuck"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163590,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164590,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If all goes well, and if I’ve done my math\nright, then when I bump the table, the rocket"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168240,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the pendulum should sway a lot less than\nthe rocket without."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171540,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see, the tuned mass damper does\nactually help!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174660,
    "dDurationMs": 1299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(though it’s a bit subtle)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175959,
    "dDurationMs": 4561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here’s a graph of the motion of the rocket\nin each case, which makes it more obvious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180520,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And though tuned mass dampers definitely weren’t\nused in the saturn V rocket in this way (since"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185050,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is where the lunar module went), they\nare used in skyscrapers and even in other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189580,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things that aren’t buildings (though they’re\nusually hard to notice)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192970,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if you look closely at power\nlines, a lot of them have this little dumbbell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196920,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing on them, which is a tuned mass damper\nthat keeps the lines from shaking too vigorously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201220,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the wind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202220,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And tuned mass dampers have been used to reduce\nunwanted vibrations in airplane engines, formula"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206900,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1 racing cars, and audio speaker cones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210190,
    "dDurationMs": 4939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there you go – the tuned mass damper,\naka the physics of how to use little things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215129,
    "dDurationMs": 5121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to stop big things from shaking!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220250,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you've probably guessed by now, this video\nwas sponsored by LEGO - I've been a huge fan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224700,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of LEGO for pretty much my entire life, spending\nhours and hours building and rebuilding all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229090,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sorts of LEGO projects as a child and teenager,\nand even more recently sneaking some into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233290,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MinutePhysics videos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234290,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'm excited that LEGO wanted to full-on\nsponsor a video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237700,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Saturn V sets are super cleverly designed\nand really fun to build, and of course I'm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242450,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a big Apollo fan and I love how the rocket\nactually stages like the real thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246540,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, the folks at LEGO want me to point\nyou to their online and physical stores which,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251080,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "naturally, have the largest collection of\nlego sets, and also allow you to find and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254950,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buy individual pieces a la carte for custom\nprojects, get expert lego help, and with LEGO"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260560,
    "dDurationMs": 2830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VIP you can get early access to new LEGO sets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263390,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks so much to LEGO for sponsoring this\nvideo and filling my childhood with creative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268140,
    "dDurationMs": 690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "delight."
    } ]
  } ]
}
